claim:
needs:
title: Match closed-ness relative to .pidly, not on the absolute path
effort: S
area: cli

Closed-ness is matched as "the path contains /c/" in two places, against a
path that starts at the checkout root: the dependency scan in cmd_claim
(case $_dp in */c/*) and the closed[] test in survey's awk ($2 ~ /\/c\//).
A checkout under a directory named c — ~/c/pidly, /srv/c/proj — makes every
ticket match, so claim reports nothing blocked and list reports everything
ready. Both are wrong in the unsafe direction.

cmd_reopen and check's closed-tree rule already strip the root first
(${_path#"$_r"/}) and match c/* or */c/*. Do the same here, or give the two
callers one helper so the rule is written once.

Done when the two sites match relative to .pidly and a test runs the suite
from a checkout whose path contains a c segment.
